ation","data_points":[{"x":"0","y":"-15","z":"90"}],"uuid":"3e4d5f84-19a8-5258-bc00-5bc0fabacc91","time":1.6,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"0","y":"0","z":"0"}],"uuid":"cc3a29ae-d606-55df-94e4-7a1f75145c31","time":0,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"0","y":"0","z":"0"}],"uuid":"b12f7083-b46d-57ff-a363-3dc3a950e964","time":0.25,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"-23.5","y":"-13.004","z":"4"}],"uuid":"01527ee3-1f2a-54df-9ebe-0d3a6fdecc24","time":0.75,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"-23.03","y":"-12.744","z":"3.92"}],"uuid":"83964c27-5f5d-528f-bb3b-73410c064494","time":0.88,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"-23.5","y":"-13.004","z":"4"}],"uuid":"15bfd024-575f-55d8-af87-56b70d543b86","time":1,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"-23.5","y":"-13.004","z":"4"}],"uuid":"7e460235-451a-5333-8faf-c46bb5f041a3","time":1.6,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"}]}}}],"description":"## cannon_bronze\n\nField cannon, bronze (E1).\n\nRemade in Patch 5: a short, very thick-walled bronze barrel with heavy reinforcing rings, a thick breech and cascabel, trunnions, mouldings and dolphin handles, and a visibly small 3.5 u bore, because bronze cannot take large charges; the carriage cheeks moved out to fit it. `slot_muzzle` marks the muzzle mouth for the flash, sparks and smoke.\n\n- Cubes: 61, all in `finished`; no hidden state sets (the construction and ruined sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in the Patch 5 remake; the game draws none of them for buildings).\n- Bounds at rest: x -14.0..14.0, y 0.0..39.0, z -32.1..34.0 (size 28.0 x 39.0 x 66.1 u = 79 x 110 x 186 cm).\nField cannon: about 1.8 m long with the trail (66 u), barrel 1.2 m, wheels 1.1 m. Short, thick bronze barrel (1.2 m = 42.7 u, warm golden-brown) with a flared cast muzzle ring, a heavier reinforce with two lion-face mouldings near the breech, base ring and cascabel knob, on an oak two-wheeled carriage with iron straps and cap-squares, a sloping trail with an iron shoe and lunette, a team-colour stripe along the trail, 1.1 m spoked wheels with iron tyres, and a sponge bucket hanging from the trail.\nHauled field gun, faces -Z (muzzle forward), stands on y = 0 on its wheels and trail shoe.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 28 x 39 x 66 u (w x h x d), centred x = 0, z = 1, from y = 0.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `carriage` (pivot at the trail shoe, so the fire hop rocks on the trail) > `barrel` (pivot at the trunnions, pitch = elevation; the game may set it directly to aim) > `fx_muzzle` (empty, at the muzzle mouth: spawn flash/smoke/ball here), `wheel_r`, `wheel_l` (pivots on the axle), `bucket` (sponge bucket).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the trail-end lunette (the limber or the animal's draw-bar hooks here; guns are towed trail-first), `slot_crew_1` = loader/rammer, standing 40 u in front of the muzzle, slightly right, facing +Z back toward the muzzle (the dwarf crew's `ram` key reaches ~40 u forward and ~20 u up), `slot_crew_2` = gunner beside the trail on the left, facing -Z. Crew slots sit on the ground (y = 0) and are children of `root` so they do not jump with the gun.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` is designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s, ox/horse walk): the wheels make one turn per 3.44 s (circumference 122.5 u). `move` rolls the wheels for travel toward -Z (muzzle first, crew man-handling it); `move_towed` rolls them the other way for travel toward +Z (trail first behind the animal). Scale the clip speed for other speeds.\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.08 s (the flash: spawn the ball at `fx_muzzle`); the gun jumps back 10.7 u (30 cm) by 0.4 s with a hop and wheel roll, settles, and the crew run it back into battery from 1.5 s to 2.4 s. `reload` key 2.4 s (loaded; the barrel is levelled for loading 0.5-2.4 s, then relaid). `aim` loops an elevation sweep. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with a wobbling left wheel. `destroyed` holds: the right wheel breaks off and falls flat, the carriage drops onto its broken side, the barrel tips off its trunnions.\n\n**Props:** rammer and powder ladle for the crew are separate files in `cannon_rammer/`.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `move_towed` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `fire` | 2.4 | once |\n| `reload` | 3 | once |\n| `aim` | 3 | loop |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.6 | hold |\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `fx_muzzle` at (0, 25.5, -27.2)\n- `slot_muzzle` at (0, 25.5, -27.2)\n- `slot_hitch` at (0, 3.5, 34)\n- `slot_crew_1` at (6, 0, -72)\n- `slot_crew_2` at (-12, 0, 19)"}